  "id": "fascia",
  "term": "fascia",
  "definition": "Fascia is the body-wide network of connective tissue that surrounds, links, and supports muscles, organs, nerves, joints, bones, and other soft tissues. In current usage, it refers to a continuous three-dimensional matrix that includes structures such as tendons, ligaments, bursae, and the connective tissue layers around muscles.",
